From ddf9f58df71da49fe99d7adf02c7d330f26d0cc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] kk: Keep the MSL of compiled pipelines compressed

Every pipeline keeps the MSL of its stages to serialize itself, the vertex
shader object a second copy of the fragment shader's. Horizon Zero Dawn
creates about 23000 pipelines while loading, which held some 9 GB of MSL
and pushed a 16 GB Mac into swap. Once the Metal pipelines exist, compress
the MSL with LZFSE from Apple's libcompression, about 6.5 times smaller
for 1 ms per 225 KB under Rosetta, and inflate it only to serialize.

Generated-by: LLM
